{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792832411,"nonce":"DcoT0e8rJgS+gF5Vyc6ZoG8DYL8=","title":"diag: compile errors and failed reloads as structured diagnostics","message":"Runtime errors reach a host as `caribou::diag::Diagnostic` (kind, message, labels with lang, module, byte span, notes, cause). Compile errors don't:\n- a failed reload arrives as `Event::Reload { error: Option\u003cString\u003e }`, a string;\n- Wren's compile errors come through its VM error callback (module, line, message);\n- Zyntax frontends render their own ariadne text.\n\nChimpMonk's editor needs every finding a guest produces as data it can list and jump to: code, module, span, message.\n\nWanted:\n- Each adapter turns its language's compile diagnostics into the same `Diagnostic` shape, one per finding.\n- `Event::Reload` carries `Vec\u003cDiagnostic\u003e` instead of the string.\n- `World::load`/import failures do the same.","files":null}]}